// B2 course (B1 → B2 roadmap), module 2 „Linn, teenused ja asjaajamine” (b1b2-006…010), stage B1+.
// Design v4 „task-based” (docs/COURSE_DESIGN_STATIONS.md §7, owner 2026-11-17) on the v3 station engine, built like the
// sample module 1 (b2/module01.js). Module goal (the learner): „Ma oskan oma linnas asju ajada”: find the right place,
// ask politely, complain so that he is heard and keep his head when the plan changes. Module product „Minu linna
// abikaart” (010 Kasuta), presented in the S1 talk of the check. Every teaching lesson follows one arc in exactly 4
// stations (≤ 75 min of a 90-min lesson):
//   1 hook + pre-task (≤ 80 words, the learner answers in the first minute) → 2 input + task → 3 language focus
//   (notice → rule → use) → 4 product in class + „Kui aega jääb” + exit check (3 items) + „Ma oskan …”;
//   the long writing and a 1-minute voice message are homework; the lesson words reach „Harjuta” through
//   vocabulary/lessonWords/b1b2.json (Sõnavara → Teemad → Moodul 2).
// One format and one everyday topic a lesson, no two neighbours alike (admin/course/v4Tasks.test.js):
//   006 game    „Kuhu sa lähed, kui pass on kadunud?”            town         final explain: the way for a new neighbour
//   007 infogap „Kas ma saaksin aja juba täna?”                    health       final negotiate: an appointment by phone
//   008 case    „Kolm kuud ja katki — kas kaebad?”                 money        final complain: a complaint to the seller (W13)
//   009 project „Homme pole vett — mis on sinu plaan B?”           neighbours   final plan: the house's plan B (S17 + notice)
//   010 exam    Kontroll 2 in Harno B2 form (kept, cast-free) + „Minu linna abikaart” as the S1 one-minute talk.
// Grammar line of the module (B1, by discovery, spiralled): kus? kuhu? kust? inner and outer local cases (006), the
// conditional in polite requests and the negative question with the partitive (007), cause and effect — kuna, sest,
// seetõttu, mistõttu, … tõttu, tänu — and the defect as a partial subject (008), reacting to change — kui …, sel
// juhul, selle asemel, et …, Kas see tähendab, et …? (009). The one long text of the module (the topic opener, ≈ 330
// words) is in 006 station 2, after a 15-minute hook. Exam corners (COURSE_FINAL_SHAPE_B2 §6): 006 R3 (cloze of local
// cases), 007 S1 (the home talk at a meeting), 008 W1 (the complaint), 009 S2 (argument cards). The course's cast is
// not used; the old storyline (the Mets family's flat) is in archive/v3/b2/module02.js and the v2 version in git history.
import { B, tag, teach, withShapes } from '../blocks.js';
import { exitCheck, extension, homeTask, purpose, station } from '../stationBlocks.js';

// a talk with the teacher as the partner, done in the lesson (engine/inLesson.js), not a home recording
const inLesson = (block) => ({ ...block, inLesson: true });
// the lesson's grammar as the small subtitle under the title on every sheet
const grammar = (text) => ({
  discover: { label: '1 Avasta', slot: 1, subtitle: text },
  practice: { label: '2 Harjuta', slot: 2, subtitle: text },
  transfer: { label: '3 Kasuta', slot: 3, subtitle: text },
});
// the home task card at the end of every lesson
const homework = (id, items) => B.phrasebank(id, [['Kodutöö', items]]);
const WORDS_HOME = 'Tunni sõnad: Sõnavara → Teemad → Moodul 2. Kui teema on läbitud, kordad sõnu „Harjuta” all.';
// a learner who cannot record (no quiet room, no smartphone) says the talk at the start of the next lesson
const NO_RECORDING = 'Kui salvestada ei saa, räägi see järgmise tunni alguses õpetajale.';

// used by the check lesson 010
// an exam part header carries the goal of its part: b2/lessonGoals.test.js asks every non-text block of a B2 sheet for one
// of the lesson's goals, and the header has none of its own (B.examPart: goal '')
const PART = (id, skill, o) => ({ ...B.examPart(id, skill, o), goal: ['R', 'L'].includes(skill) ? 'g_read' : 'g_use' });
// the examiner's set with its own instruction (B.examiner's default wording is shared by every module: finalShape V7)
const withInstruction = (b, instruction) => ({ ...b, data: { ...b.data, instruction } });
